# Alembic migrations

## Rules

1. **Alembic only**, under `apps/api/migrations/versions/`.
2. **Never edit a shipped migration**; files already in git history are immutable. Add a new revision.
3. Hook enforcement: `guard-shipped-migrations.sh` blocks edits to existing files under `versions/`.

## Workflow

```bash
pnpm run db:migrate:new   # autogenerate, always review the diff
pnpm run db:migrate       # local upgrade head
```

## Autogenerate review checklist

- [ ] `workspace_id NOT NULL` + RLS policy (`FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) on every tenant table (`workspace-scoping`)
- [ ] Indexes on FK columns used in list queries; `workspace_id` leading in composite indexes
- [ ] Extensions (`vector`, `pg_trgm`, `pgcrypto`) enabled in an explicit migration
- [ ] No accidental drops without an explicit plan
- [ ] Downgrade path sane (or document one-way)
- [ ] Runs under the migration role; app role keeps no `BYPASSRLS`

Skills: `alembic-migrations`, `fix-migration-issues`, `workspace-scoping`.
